== Notes ==
* Just like {{e|Mom}} and Mom's Heart, using {{i|The Bible}} or {{p|XV - The Devil?}} against It Lives! will kill it instantly.
* {{dlc|a}} Isaac can encounter It Lives! in the nightmare boss wave of chapter 4 in [[Greed mode|Greed/Greedier mode]] even if it has not been unlocked.

== Trivia ==
* It Lives! appeared in the original ''The Binding of Isaac.''  Unlike its appearance in Rebirth, It Lives! had opened eyes, a simple poker face, and hung to the ceiling in a sideways position via an umbilical cord.
* The music that plays during this fight is titled ''Ventricide''.<ref>http://ridiculon.bandcamp.com/</ref> Ventricide is a portmanteau formed from the word ventricle (chamber of the heart) and the suffix -cide, which denotes an act of killing. This theme is used in other tracks, such as Matricide, Hericide, and Infanticide.
** Ventricide could also be a junction of the prefix ''ventr-'' (from the latin word ''venter''), which could denote "belly", "stomach", "womb" or "fetus", with the suffix ''-cide''.
** It Lives! shares this theme with Mom's Heart, and therefore, both interpretations could co-exist.
* It Lives!, according to the developers, takes the shape of what Isaac looked like as a fetus.
* According to Edmund McMillen, It Lives! supposedly represents Isaac wishing that he were never born.
* It Lives! makes the same sounds as Mom's Heart.
** Like Mom's Heart, if Isaac takes damage from It Lives!' {{i|Brimstone}} attack, Mom's laugh can be heard.
* Despite being a major boss, It Lives! isn't linked to any [[Endings|Ending]], instead, it opens up entrances to both {{s|Sheol}} and the {{s|Cathedral}}, as well as {{s|???}} if beaten in under 30 minutes.
* The unlock note for It Lives! states "Your futures past awaits.", referencing ''Time Fcuk'', another game by Edmund Mcmillen.
* {{dlc|nr}} During the versus screen, It Lives!' enemy/boss-spawning sound can be heard. It Lives! is one of {{Dlc|nr}}seven/{{Dlc|r}}five bosses that can be heard during the versus screen, the other {{Dlc|nr}}six/{{Dlc|r}}four being {{e|The Stain}}, {{e|The Forsaken}}, {{e|Big Horn}}, Mom, {{dlc|nr}} Mom's Heart and {{e|Mother}}.

